{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213906,"nonce":"TMw/6VMJAv6TuZ4KaA3hHBpQfP0=","title":"Immix collector as a fourth GcAllocator strategy (block/line/TLAB, non-moving)","message":"New src/runtime/gc_immix.rs behind GcAllocator, selectable with --gc immix, so it can be built and measured next to the generational default without touching callers.\n\n- Geometry: 32 KiB blocks, 128 B lines, 16 B quantum. Heap is one block-aligned reservation (mmap on unix, alloc_zeroed elsewhere), size from WLIFT_GC_HEAP_MB else usable_ram/4 clamped [512 MiB, 4 GiB] on 64-bit; smaller default on wasm32.\n- Side tables keyed by heap offset: `objects` one byte per quantum (0 = not a start, 1..8 = small object of code*16 bytes, 9 = line-aligned span whose size is alloc_sizes[line]*128; bit 7 = mark), `alloc_sizes` u32 per line, `Block { line_marks: [u64; 4], has_span, any_marked }`. No collector state in the object header.\n- Allocation: TLAB bump for objects \u003c= 128 B (never straddle a line; publish start byte before advancing cursor), line-aligned spans for larger, contiguous-block runs for \u003e 32 KiB. Refill takes recycled line spans first, then a free block, else collect then retry. Trigger accounting per region.\n- Interior pointers resolve through containing_allocation (walk back within the line, then across alloc_sizes gated by has_span).\n- Marking is object-granular; line bits are set per covered line for sweep only. Heap tracing stays precise via the existing trace_object walk (objects hold NaN-boxed Values, so conservative word scanning inside the heap would miss them).\n- Sweep walks object starts per used block: dead objects run drop_in_place_by_type and unlink_intern (payloads are still malloc'd Rust values), then start bytes clear; lines with no marks become recycle spans; blocks with none stay free; untouched blocks skip mark clearing. Hand back free blocks to the OS only when the last collection is older than a heartbeat, keep a small resident float, MADV_FREE_REUSABLE on macOS with the reuse ledger.\n- Triggers: bytes_since_gc + external \u003e= threshold, threshold = clamp(live * growth, floor, ceiling); 30 s heartbeat; WLIFT_GC_STRESS keeps the bump path on (Ash's stress mode disables TLAB, which hides rooting bugs under reuse).\n- write_barrier is an inlined no-op; collect(roots) uses the precise root vector the VM already builds. Nothing moves, so writeback is identity.\n- for_each_fiber walks starts of ObjType::Fiber.\n\n- lib + e2e + aot suites pass with --gc immix; e2e MarkSweep-strategy tests gain an Immix variant.\n- binary_trees at depth 14 and 16 measured against generational; target is parity or better before conservative scanning lands.","files":null}]}